

<div class="container-fluid pb-5">
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col">
            <h2 class="fw-bold mb-0">Advanced SQL Guide</h2>
            <p class="text-secondary small">Deep dives into window functions, concurrency, and dynamic SQL</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Window Functions & CTEs -->
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="card bg-dark border-primary border-2 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-header bg-primary text-white border-bottom border-primary">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Window Functions & CTEs</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h6 class="text-primary fw-bold">Common Table Expressions (CTEs)</h6>
                    <p class="text-light">CTEs simplify complex queries by breaking them into logical blocks.</p>
                    <pre class="bg-black text-success p-3 rounded border border-secondary"><code>WITH SalesCTE AS (
    SELECT EmployeeID, SUM(TotalAmount) as TotalSales
    FROM Sales
    GROUP BY EmployeeID
)
SELECT e.Name, s.TotalSales
FROM Employees e
JOIN SalesCTE s ON e.EmployeeID = s.EmployeeID
WHERE s.TotalSales > 10000;</code></pre>

                    <h6 class="text-info fw-bold mt-4">Window Functions: ROW_NUMBER()</h6>
                    <p class="text-light">Find the latest order for each customer without a self-join:</p>
                    <pre class="bg-black text-success p-3 rounded border border-secondary"><code>WITH RankedOrders AS (
    SELECT 
        OrderID, 
        CustomerID, 
        OrderDate,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER(PARTITION BY CustomerID ORDER BY OrderDate DESC) as rn
    FROM Orders
)
SELECT * FROM RankedOrders WHERE rn = 1;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Temp Tables vs Table Variables vs CTEs -->
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="card bg-dark border-info border-2 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-header bg-info text-dark border-bottom border-info">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Temp Tables vs Table Variables vs CTEs</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table class="table table-dark table-striped table-hover">
                            <thead class="table-info text-dark">
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Feature</th>
                                    <th>#TempTable</th>
                                    <th>@("@TableVariable")</th>
                                    <th>CTE</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Best For</td>
                                    <td>Large intermediate datasets</td>
                                    <td>Small datasets (&lt; 100 rows)</td>
                                    <td>Structuring queries, recursion</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Can have Indexes?</td>
                                    <td>Yes</td>
                                    <td>Only Primary Key / Unique</td>
                                    <td>No</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Scope</td>
                                    <td>Session (or proc execution)</td>
                                    <td>Batch / Proc</td>
                                    <td>Single query statement</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>Triggers Recompiles?</td>
                                    <td>Yes (updates statistics)</td>
                                    <td>No</td>
                                    <td>No</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Dynamic SQL & Security -->
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="card bg-dark border-warning border-2 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-header bg-warning text-dark border-bottom border-warning">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Dynamic SQL & SQL Injection Prevention</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <p class="text-light">Never concatenate strings directly for execution. Always use <code>sp_executesql</code>.</p>
                    <h6 class="text-danger fw-bold">❌ Bad (Vulnerable to Injection)</h6>
                    <pre class="bg-black text-success p-3 rounded border border-secondary"><code>DECLARE @@sql NVARCHAR(MAX) = 'SELECT * FROM Users WHERE Username = ''' + @@UserInput + '''';
EXEC(@@sql);</code></pre>
                    <h6 class="text-success fw-bold mt-3">✅ Good (Parameterized Dynamic SQL)</h6>
                    <pre class="bg-black text-success p-3 rounded border border-secondary"><code>DECLARE @@sql NVARCHAR(MAX) = N'SELECT * FROM Users WHERE Username = @@User';
EXEC sp_executesql 
    @@stmt = @@sql, 
    @@params = N'@@User NVARCHAR(50)', 
    @@User = @@UserInput;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Transactions & Deadlocks -->
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="card bg-dark border-danger border-2 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-header bg-danger text-white border-bottom border-danger">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Transactions & Deadlocks</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h6 class="text-danger fw-bold">Deadlock Prevention Strategy</h6>
                    <p class="text-light">A deadlock happens when two processes lock resources each other needs. To prevent this:</p>
                    <ul class="text-light">
                        <li>Always access tables in the <strong>same order</strong> across all stored procedures.</li>
                        <li>Keep transactions as short as possible.</li>
                        <li>Avoid user interaction during a transaction.</li>
                        <li>Use lower isolation levels if applicable, such as <code>SNAPSHOT</code> isolation.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <h6 class="text-warning fw-bold mt-4">Transaction Template with Error Handling</h6>
                    <pre class="bg-black text-success p-3 rounded border border-secondary"><code>BEGIN TRY
    BEGIN TRANSACTION;
    
    -- DB operations here
    UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance - 100 WHERE ID = 1;
    UPDATE Accounts SET Balance = Balance + 100 WHERE ID = 2;
    
    COMMIT TRANSACTION;
END TRY
BEGIN CATCH
    IF @@TRANCOUNT > 0
        ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;
        
    -- Log or re-throw error
    THROW;
END CATCH;</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Data Types -->
    <div class="row mb-4">
        <div class="col-12">
            <div class="card bg-dark border-success border-2 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-header bg-success text-white border-bottom border-success">
                    <h5 class="mb-0">Data Type Choices & Storage Optimization</h5>
                </div>
                <div class="card-body">
                    <div class="list-group list-group-flush">
                        <div class="list-group-item bg-transparent text-light border-bottom border-secondary">
                            <h6 class="text-success fw-bold">VARCHAR vs NVARCHAR</h6>
                            <p class="mb-1">Only use <code>NVARCHAR</code> if you need to store Unicode (multi-language) characters. <code>NVARCHAR</code> takes 2 bytes per character, doubling your storage space and memory usage compared to <code>VARCHAR</code>.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="list-group-item bg-transparent text-light border-bottom border-secondary">
                            <h6 class="text-success fw-bold">DATETIME vs DATETIME2</h6>
                            <p class="mb-1">Always prefer <code>DATETIME2</code>. It has a larger date range, higher fractional second precision, and often uses less storage space (6-8 bytes vs 8 bytes).</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="list-group-item bg-transparent text-light">
                            <h6 class="text-success fw-bold">Avoid GUIDs for Clustered Indexes</h6>
                            <p class="mb-1">Using <code>NEWID()</code> (GUIDs) as a Primary Key/Clustered Index causes massive index fragmentation because the values are completely random, forcing SQL Server to constantly split pages. If you must use a GUID, use <code>NEWSEQUENTIALID()</code> or create a separate <code>INT IDENTITY</code> column for the clustered index.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

